# Later rules win, so the general case goes first and the exceptions follow.
* text=auto

# Recorded agent output is byte-pinned evidence, not source.
#
# `tests/provenance.test.ts` fails a fixture whose md5 or size stops matching
# the table in its README, which is what stops a hand-edited "recording" from
# passing review. With `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default — git was
# rewriting every LF in these files on checkout, so the bytes on disk were not
# the bytes that were recorded, and provenance failed for anyone who cloned.
#
# Found the first time these files went through a real checkout: eight lines,
# eight extra bytes.
*.ndjson -text
